# REQ-002: Electronic Inbound Ingestion

**Priority:** Must Have
**Effort:** High
**Risk:** High
**Depends On:** REQ-001 (Unified Inbound Document Inbox)

---

## User Story

As a practice administrator,
I need all inbound electronic document sources to be consolidated into the inbox automatically,
So that I never have to monitor multiple systems or miss documents arriving via any channel.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] All seven inbound sources are supported: MESH, MIG, FHIR, Docman Connect, NHSmail, EDT, 111.
- [ ] Documents from all active sources appear in the unified inbox without manual intervention.
- [ ] When one or more sources are unavailable, documents from working sources are still displayed in the inbox.
- [ ] Source availability status is tracked operationally, but no user-facing source-availability banner is shown in this release.
- [ ] Lack of source-availability banner does not block the user from triaging and processing documents from functioning sources.
- [ ] When an unavailable source recovers, its documents are ingested automatically without requiring user intervention.
- [ ] Source identity is preserved as metadata on each document (populated in the "Source" triage field from REQ-001). NHSmail-sourced documents are labelled **NHSmail** in the source chip.
- [ ] **NHSmail source — email body viewer:** For documents arriving via NHSmail, the document viewer displays a structured email header block (From, To, Subject, Date) and the full email body text above the attached clinical document. The email body and the attached document are presented as a continuous view, separated by a clearly labelled divider. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] **NHSmail source — attachment handling:** Where an NHSmail carries one or more attached clinical documents, each attachment is identified by name, file type, and size. The workflow (file, code, task) is applied to the attached clinical document, not to the email body itself. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] **NHSmail source — email-only messages:** Where an NHSmail carries no attachment (email body is the entire clinical content), the email body is treated as the document to be filed. The document type is pre-populated as "Email — Clinical" and the user must confirm before filing. *(Must Have)*

