## Dimension 1: Clinical Safety

### Applicable Guardrails
- **CLIN-007:** Hazard Mitigation Evidence — source unavailability must be explicitly detectable via operational telemetry and logs in this release
- **CLIN-009:** Clinical Safety Logging — source failure events logged using structured identifiers
- **CLIN-010:** Error Handling Patient Safety — fail open per source (not per inbox); inbox never silently appears complete when a source is down

### Hazards Addressed

- **HAZ-DOC-005:** Clinical document not received due to silent source failure — practice unaware documents are missing
  - **Severity:** Critical
  - **Likelihood:** Medium
  - **Risk Level:** Critical

- **HAZ-DOC-006:** Practice assumes inbox is complete when one or more sources are down — clinical decisions made on incomplete information
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Medium
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-007:** Documents from recovered source ingested out of order or duplicated after outage
  - **Severity:** Medium
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** Medium

### Mitigations

- **MIT-DOC-004:** Source availability status is recorded in structured telemetry and logs, and monitored by operations alerts; no user-facing source warning banner is shown in this release
  - **Type:** Monitoring / Observability
  - **Effectiveness:** Partial (operations visibility retained; user-visible awareness deferred)

- **MIT-DOC-005:** Structured source-failure events logged with source identifier, failure onset timestamp, and recovery timestamp
  - **Type:** Monitoring / Observability
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-006:** Deduplication logic applied on ingestion to prevent duplicate documents after source recovery
  - **Type:** Business Logic
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

