## Dimension 2: Information Governance

### Applicable Guardrails
- **IG-001:** Data Minimisation — ingestion pipeline captures only document content and required metadata; no extraneous fields from source systems
- **IG-003:** Lawful Basis Declaration — Article 6(1)(e) public task + Article 9(2)(h) health data
- **IG-004:** Special Category Data Protection — documents in transit encrypted (TLS 1.2+); at rest AES-256-GCM
- **IG-009:** Data Breach Notification — ingestion failure or misdirected document events must be detectable and reportable within 24hr to DPO

### Data Handling
- Source metadata (source name, ingestion timestamp) retained as document metadata
- Documents from each source treated as special category health data from point of ingestion
- NHSmail source: production access route not yet confirmed by NHS England — see Parking Lot in manifest.md (⚪ To Verify). When unblocked: email headers (From, To, Subject, Date) and body will be stored as part of the document record; email body surfaced in the document viewer alongside any attachment
- No document content stored in transit buffers beyond minimum required for ingestion processing

### GDPR Articles
- **Article 6(1)(e):** Lawful basis — public task (NHS direct care)
- **Article 9(2)(h):** Special category health data — medical purposes
- **Article 5(1)(f):** Integrity and confidentiality — appropriate security during ingestion

