## PxD (Added by V1d)

> **Scope note:** REQ-002 is a **Partial PxD**.
> - **Pre-built (external):** NHSmail email header block, email body renderer, attachment bar — these are owned by the pre-built NHSmail integration component. No layout spec is required from Document Manager.
> - **Net-new (Document Manager owned):** Stored-copy notice `Banner` component (rendered when NHSmail original is inaccessible) + real-time queue badge increment UX behaviour.
> - **Descoped:** Inbox-level source-availability banner ("NHSmail is down") — explicitly out of scope per AC v1.4 and CHECK 2.

---

### User Flow

**Primary Flow — Electronic document arrives in queue:**
1. Ingestion pipeline receives document from source (MESH, NHSmail, FHIR, etc.) — background process, no user action required
2. Queue tab badge increments in real-time (mechanism per `CONCURRENCY-001`); `aria-live="polite"` region on tab badge announces new count to screen readers
3. Admin sees new document row in Filing Queue table — source column shows source chip (e.g. "NHSmail")
4. Admin opens document — gallery view loads (standard 3-column layout per REQ-001)
5. If document is NHSmail-sourced AND original email is inaccessible: full-width `Banner` (stored-copy notice) renders above the 3-column gallery immediately on open
6. Admin reads stored-copy notice; continues workflow normally — Match → File → Code → Task steps unaffected
7. Pre-built NHSmail component renders email header block + body + attachment bar in the centre viewer column

**Error Flow — Ingestion failure:**
1. Source adapter fails to ingest a document (parsing error, S3 write failure, etc.)
2. Document does NOT appear in the queue — no silent failure
3. Failure event emitted to telemetry (OTEL span `documents.ingestion.source_failure`) — operations alert fires
4. No user-facing error shown for ingestion failures in this release (operational monitoring only per CLIN-007)

**Exit Types:**
- Same exit types as REQ-001 primary flow (Complete / Cancel / Reject / Queue-Peek Navigate / Navigate-away)
- Stored-copy notice does not add a new exit type — it is informational only

