### Component Specifications

> 🚫 All components use `@emisgroup/ui-*` exclusively.

**Stored-Copy Notice Banner:**
- Component: `Banner` from `@emisgroup/ui-banner`
- `variant="warning"` — cautionary but non-blocking
- Content: `{t('nhsmail.storedCopyNotice.message')}` = "You are viewing a stored copy of this document. The original email is no longer accessible."
- Dismiss: optional close `Button variant="mono" circular ariaLabel={t('nhsmail.storedCopyNotice.dismiss')}` — dismissal is session-only (banner returns on next gallery open for same document)
- Placement: rendered by Document Manager gallery wrapper above the 3-column layout; `position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 10` so it remains visible on scroll
- Condition: shown only when `document.sourceChannel === 'nhsmail' && document.originalAccessible === false`
- ARIA: `role="region" aria-label={t('nhsmail.storedCopyNotice.region')}` on wrapper; `Banner` component provides `role="status"` internally
- Keyboard: dismiss button reachable via Tab; Enter/Space dismisses

**Real-Time Queue Badge (UX behaviour — mechanism per CONCURRENCY-001):**
- Component: `Count` badge on `Tabs.Tab` (already specified in REQ-001)
- On new document arrival: badge count increments; `aria-live="polite"` on tab label announces `t('inbox.tab.newDocument', { count })` to screen readers
- Visual: no additional animation on increment (clinical data — avoid distracting motion, consistent with REQ-001 decision)
- Implementation dependency: `CONCURRENCY-001` must resolve WebSocket / SSE / polling mechanism before V3 coding

---

### Interaction Patterns

**Stored-copy banner dismiss:**
- Trigger: click/Enter/Space on dismiss `Button`
- Result: `Banner` removed from DOM for current session; `sessionStorage` key set to suppress re-render for document GUID within session
- On next gallery open for same document: banner reappears (session-only suppression)

**Real-time badge increment:**
- Trigger: inbound event received via `CONCURRENCY-001` channel
- Result: `Count` badge re-renders with new value; `aria-live` region fires
- No row insertion animation in queue table — new document appears on next tab visit or manual refresh (incremental row push is out of scope for this release)

